Adapt RDO's rpm-master python-os-traits.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(os-traits 3.6.0, the version pinned by the 2026.1 upper-constraints).

PEP 625 changed how Python sdists are named: upstream now publishes
os_traits-3.6.0.tar.gz, which unpacks into os_traits-3.6.0/. The spec still
builds both the filename and the setup directory from the hyphenated project
name, so the build dies immediately:

    cd os-traits-3.6.0
    /var/tmp/rpm-tmp.4Ry5xa: line 44: cd: os-traits-3.6.0: No such file or directory

build-rpms.sh already saves the download under whatever filename the spec asks
for, so only the unpack directory needs correcting here. The spec defines both
names already - sname for the project, pypi_name for the distribution - so this
just uses the right one.

diff -ur a/os-traits/python-os-traits.spec b/os-traits/python-os-traits.spec
--- a/python-os-traits.spec	2026-09-28 22:18:57
+++ b/python-os-traits.spec	2026-09-28 22:30:12
@@ -78,7 +78,10 @@
 %if 0%{?sources_gpg} == 1
 %{gpgverify}  --keyring=%{SOURCE102} --signature=%{SOURCE101} --data=%{SOURCE0}
 %endif
-%autosetup -n %{sname}-%{upstream_version} -S git
+# PEP 625: upstream now publishes os_traits-X.tar.gz, which unpacks into
+# os_traits-X/, while sname is still the hyphenated project name. Use the
+# distribution name for the directory.
+%autosetup -n %{pypi_name}-%{upstream_version} -S git
 # Remove bundled egg-info
 rm -rf %{pypi_name}.egg-info
 
